# Pairs with ListedInSink. Production before the fix of #5418: a full
# backup's id was the hash of its payload alone, so a full capture of an
# unchanged tree republished an existing backup's id. A pass that had listed
# and doomed that backup removed its row and deleted its sink manifest, the
# republishing capture registered the row again (with no row left to
# reconcile against), and the catalog listed a backup the sink no longer held.
# The mutation adds a branch to Start: a full capture may take the id of a
# full backup already in the sink instead of a fresh one.
MODULE: ListedInSinkRepublishedId
TARGET: ListedInSink
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a full capture republishes an existing full backup's id
PERTURBS: Start

--- FIND
    /\ meta' = [meta EXCEPT ![next] = [kind |-> k, base |-> b, t |-> now]]
    /\ cap' = [cap EXCEPT ![c] = [ph |-> "drain", id |-> next]]
    /\ next' = next + 1
--- REPLACE
    /\ \/ /\ meta' = [meta EXCEPT ![next] = [kind |-> k, base |-> b, t |-> now]]
          /\ cap' = [cap EXCEPT ![c] = [ph |-> "drain", id |-> next]]
          /\ next' = next + 1
       \* MUTATION: a full capture of unchanged content republishes the id.
       \/ /\ k = "full"
          /\ \E r \in snk :
                /\ meta[r].kind = "full"
                /\ cap' = [cap EXCEPT ![c] = [ph |-> "drain", id |-> r]]
          /\ UNCHANGED <<meta, next>>
--- END
